; hub75.loom
; A HUB75 RGB LED matrix panel driver: 32 x 16 pixels at 1/8 scan, three
; bit planes of binary-coded modulation (8 levels per colour, 512 colours),
; refreshed from a frame buffer in the data memory, which the host loads
; with the image or updates through INQ[0] while the panel refreshes.
;
; Written on 2026-11-07, after the hardware was complete (D-032), as a
; protocol Loom was not designed for (D-035). Two threads, one per half of
; the job, and no bit engine. It uses:
;   - the deadline-latched pin write (SEMANTICS 6.10, D-016), built for
;     clock-exact UART and WS2812 edges: both OE edges of every bit plane
;     are staged and land on deadlines, so the time the LEDs are lit is
;     exactly W_p ticks whatever the other thread does, and the 1:2:4
;     weights of the planes are exact to the clock;
;   - LD/ST on the instruction memory (6.11, D-027), built for the 24C02
;     emulation: the frame buffer is 384 words of it;
;   - the barrel (section 2) and the shared flags (6.5): thread 0 shifts
;     the next bit plane while thread 1 holds the current one lit, with a
;     two-flag handshake between them;
;   - OUT on a seven-pin group: six colour bits and CLK low in one write.
; What the firmware does that no hardware does: the whole panel protocol,
; the row scan, the bit-plane schedule, the blanking around every address
; and latch change, and the tear-free update from the host.
; Weaker than a dedicated panel controller: three planes, not 8 to 12,
; because the frame buffer has to share the 512-word memory with the code
; (a fourth plane alone would need all 512 words); one 32 x 16 panel, no
; chaining (a longer chain needs more memory, not more time); no gamma
; table (the host's levels are linear in on-time); and CLK runs at about
; 2.8 MHz within a unit at 50 MHz (one column every 4.5 slots), where FPGA
; drivers clock at 10 to 25 MHz. The refresh rate is still high: see Timing.
;
; Sources (FW_README.md and tools/protomodels/hub75.py cite them in full):
; there is no HUB75 standard. The panel side follows the secondary
; descriptions: Adafruit, "32x16 and 32x32 RGB LED Matrix", "How the
; Matrix Works" (8 interleaved sections, line n with line n+8, chosen by
; A B C; 192 bits clocked out and latched per section), and H. Zeller,
; rpi-rgb-led-matrix, wiring.md (signals R1 G1 B1 R2 G2 B2, A B C (D for
; 32 rows, 1:16), CLK, strobe = LAT, OE- active low). The column drivers
; are 74HC595-style constant-current shift registers; their timing is
; checked against TI TLC5916 (SLVS695D, revised January 2015), section
; 7.9 "Timing Requirements" and the Pin Functions table of section 6: data
; shift on CLK rising, the latch transparent while LE is high and closed
; when LE goes low, OE low enables the outputs; tw(CLK) and tw(L) 20 ns,
; tsu(D) 3 ns, th(D) 2 ns, tsu(L) and th(L) 15 ns, tw(OE) 500 ns (IOUT <
; 60 mA), 30 MHz. The ICN2037 and MBI5124 data sheets that real panels use
; could not be read (QUESTIONS.md), so the TLC5916 stands in for them.
;
; Pins (12 outputs; no pin is written by both threads):
;   thread 0  R1 G1 B1 R2 G2 B2 = BIDIR0..5, CLK = BIDIR6 (OUT group 0..6)
;   thread 1  A B C = OUT0..2 (OUT group 16..18), LAT = OUT3,
;             OE = BIDIR7 (active low; a board pull-up keeps the panel
;             blank until thread 1 drives it: PIN_OUT resets to 0, so OE on
;             a uo pad would light the panel's power-up garbage from reset
;             to RUN). OUT4 is free for D on a 1/16-scan panel.
; Each thread enables its own BIDIR drivers with OEP (bit-masked, 6.3).
;
; Frame buffer: 24 units of 16 words, unit u = 3 * r + p for row pair r
; (rows r and r + 8, address r on A B C) and bit plane p. Word k of a unit
; holds two columns in shift order: bits 5:0 are R1 G1 B1 R2 G2 B2 of
; column 31 - 2k, bits 13:8 those of column 30 - 2k, bit p of each pixel's
; 3-bit level; bits 7:6 and 15:14 must be 0 (bit 6 is CLK in the OUT).
; Column 31 is shifted first: after 32 clocks it is at the far end of the
; chain. Units 0..4 are at 0x030..0x07F, units 5..23 at 0x0A0..0x1CF: the
; logical word a (0..383) is at 0x030 + a, plus 0x20 from 0x080 on, to step
; over thread 1's code. The image below holds a test pattern; threads 2
; and 3 must not be started (their reset vectors are frame buffer).
;
; Host words, INQ[0], optional, two per update: the logical address a
; (0..383; larger ones are dropped with their word), then the word. Thread
; 0 stores it between two units, never while it shifts one, so no bit
; plane is ever torn; an update lands within one plane time and a gap
; (at most 2,624 clocks, 52 us at 50 MHz). Push both words together:
; thread 0 waits for the second.
; Nothing is reported on OUTQ.
;
; Timing (tick 16 clocks, set by thread 1 itself: the host must not set
; thread 1's TICK_INT; thread 0 needs no tick): plane p is lit for
; W0 * 2^p ticks, 640, 1280 and 2560 clocks; between two planes OE is high
; for 64 clocks (the scanner's handshake, the address, the LAT pulse and
; GAP ticks). Thread 0 shifts a unit in 151 slots (604 clocks: 16 words of
; 9 slots, LD being two) while the previous one is lit, so it is ready
; before the shortest plane ends. A row pair takes 4,672 clocks and a
; frame 8 of them, 37,376 clocks: 1.34 kHz at 50 MHz, lit 95.9 % of the
; time (of its 1/8 share). If a unit is late (a host update in the way),
; OE simply stays high longer: no plane is ever lit for less or more than
; its W_p ticks.
; Thread 0 (47 words) and thread 1 (26) take 73 words; with the 384-word
; frame buffer the image uses 457 of the 512.
; Start both threads together (RUN 0b0011) with SFLAGS 0 and 1 clear.
;
; Readings taken on the open spec questions (2026-11-07):
;   Driver timing: checked against the TI TLC5916 data sheet as a stand-in;
;   the ICN2037 and MBI5124 data sheets the panels use could not be read.
;   Every measured interval has a large margin over the TLC5916 minimums.
;   Shift direction: the first bit clocked in ends at column 31. A panel
;   wired the other way shows the image mirrored; reorder the frame buffer.
;   OE is on BIDIR7 with a board pull-up, so the panel is blank from reset
;   to RUN. That panels accept 3.3 V inputs is from memory, unchecked.

        .imem   512
        .equ    W0 = 40                 ; plane 0's on-time, ticks (<= 63)
        .equ    TICK = 16               ; thread 1's tick, clocks
        .equ    GAP = 2                 ; latch to OE low, ticks (>= 2)
        .equ    FB_A = 0x030            ; units 0..4
        .equ    HOLE = 0x080            ; thread 1's code
        .equ    FB_B = 0x0A0            ; units 5..23
        .equ    FB_WORDS = 384
        .equ    READY = 0               ; shared flag: a unit is shifted
        .equ    LATCHED = 1             ; shared flag: it has been latched
        .pins   R1 = BIDIR0, G1 = BIDIR1, B1 = BIDIR2
        .pins   R2 = BIDIR3, G2 = BIDIR4, B2 = BIDIR5, CLK = BIDIR6
        .pins   ADDR_A = OUT0, LAT = OUT3, OE = BIDIR7

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- thread 0
; The shifter. r0 frame-buffer pointer, r1 word, r2 words left in the
; unit, r3 units left in the frame, r4 HOLE, r5 the data mask, r6 the
; host's address, r7 FB_WORDS.
        .thread 0
shifter:
        OEP     R1, 1
        OEP     G1, 1
        OEP     B1, 1
        OEP     R2, 1
        OEP     G2, 1
        OEP     B2, 1
        OEP     CLK, 1
        .csr    OUTGRP, (7 << 5) | 0, r7        ; BIDIR0..6
        LDI     r4, HOLE
        MOV16   r5, 0x3F3F
        MOV16   r7, FB_WORDS
frame:  LDI     r0, FB_A
        LDI     r3, 24
unit:   LDI     r2, 16
col:    LD      r1, r0, 0               ; two columns
        OUT     r1                      ; column 31-2k, CLK low
        SETP    CLK, 1                  ; shift it in
        SHRI    r1, 8
        OUT     r1                      ; column 30-2k, CLK low
        SETP    CLK, 1
        ADDI    r0, 1
        DJNZ    r2, col
        CMP     r0, r4
        BNZ     shifted
        ADDI    r0, FB_B - HOLE         ; step over thread 1's code
shifted:
        SIG     READY
; Wait for the latch; meanwhile take the host's updates. SETD 0 makes the
; T forms below tests: TD is reached in the next slot.
wait:   SETD    0
        WAITS   LATCHED, T
        BNT     next                    ; latched: shift the next unit
        WAITB   INQ_NE, T
        BT      wait
        POP     r6                      ; logical address
        POP     r1                      ; the word
        CMP     r6, r7
        BC      wait                    ; past the frame buffer: dropped
        AND     r1, r1, r5              ; CLK and the spare bits stay 0
        ADDI    r6, FB_A
        CMP     r6, r4
        BNC     store
        ADDI    r6, FB_B - HOLE
store:  ST      r1, r6, 0
        JMP     wait
next:   DJNZ    r3, unit
        JMP     frame

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- thread 1
; The scanner. r1 the row pair on A B C.
        .thread 1
scanner:
        SETP    OE, 1                   ; blank before the driver is on
        OEP     OE, 1
        .csr    TICK_INT, TICK, r7
        .csr    OUTGRP, (3 << 5) | 16, r7       ; A B C = OUT0..2
        LDI     r1, 0
row:    CALL    show                    ; plane 0
        WAITD   W0                      ; OE high on this deadline
        CALL    show                    ; plane 1
        WAITD   2 * W0
        CALL    show                    ; plane 2
        WAITD   4 * W0
        ADDI    r1, 1
        ANDI    r1, 7
        JMP     row
; Latch the unit thread 0 has shifted and light it from a deadline GAP
; ticks on; the caller's WAITD ends it. OE is high throughout.
show:   WAITS   READY
        OUT     r1                      ; the row pair's address
        SETP    LAT, 1
        SETP    LAT, 0                  ; latched as LAT falls
        SIG     LATCHED                 ; thread 0 may shift the next
        SETP    OE, 0, D
        SETD    GAP                     ; OE low on this tick
        WAITD   0
        SETP    OE, 1, D                ; ...and high on the caller's
        RET

; ------------------------------------------------------------ frame buffer
; The test pattern, levels 0..7: red = x / 4, green = y / 2 (row y, 0 at
; the top), blue = 7 - x / 4. Units 0..4 follow thread 0's code, the rest
; thread 1's (tools/tests/test_fw_hub75.py, pack, builds the same).
        .thread 0
        .org    FB_A
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424   ; unit 0
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424   ; unit 1
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424
        .word   0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919   ; unit 2
        .word   0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424   ; unit 3
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424   ; unit 4
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424
        .thread 1
        .org    FB_B
        .word   0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919   ; unit 5
        .word   0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636   ; unit 6
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424   ; unit 7
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424
        .word   0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919   ; unit 8
        .word   0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636   ; unit 9
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424   ; unit 10
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x2424
        .word   0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919   ; unit 11
        .word   0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424   ; unit 12
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636   ; unit 13
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636
        .word   0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919   ; unit 14
        .word   0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424   ; unit 15
        .word   0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424, 0x0909, 0x0909, 0x2424, 0x2424
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636   ; unit 16
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636
        .word   0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919   ; unit 17
        .word   0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636   ; unit 18
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636   ; unit 19
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636
        .word   0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919   ; unit 20
        .word   0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636   ; unit 21
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636   ; unit 22
        .word   0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x1B1B, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636, 0x3636
        .word   0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919, 0x1919   ; unit 23
        .word   0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434, 0x3434
